# Only this file from ~/.ssh belongs in the repo. Keys never do: one per
# machine, generated by `setup ssh`, never copied anywhere.
#
# Two ssh traps are behind the shape of this file.
#
# For each option ssh keeps the FIRST value it finds, and IdentityFile
# accumulates across every matching block. A `Host *` block at the top
# therefore wins everything, and a host-specific key only queues up behind the
# general ones. Specific blocks go first, `Host *` last.
#
# And the attempt order comes from the AGENT, not from this file. With both
# keys loaded, ssh tried the RSA one first because it had been in the agent for
# years, whatever the order here. The fix is not to order them but to stop
# offering RSA where it is not needed: it is listed only for the hosts that
# still rely on it.

Host github.com
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
  IdentitiesOnly yes

# Hosts still authorising the old RSA key, taken from known_hosts. Remove a
# line once that host knows the machine key, and the last one to go takes the
# RSA key with it.
Host gitlab.com *.gpaas.net 192.168.1.200 192.168.1.204 homeassistant.local
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_rsa

Host *
  AddKeysToAgent yes
  UseKeychain yes
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
